<title>MEXICO: GEUPEC sees higher '96 sales, price surge in '97.</title>
<headline>GEUPEC sees higher '96 sales, price surge in '97.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican bottlers Grupo Embotelladores Unidas ended 1996 with higher sales volume and expects higher prices in 1997, a company official said Friday.</p>
<p>In 1996, the company sold 70.58 million boxes of eight ounce soft drink bottles, compared with 68.5 million boxes in 1995, company sub-director Idelfonso Ochoa Martinez told Reuters in an interview.</p>
</text>
